James inquired about the common interpretation of a “crossbar with whiskers” in R and how to adapt it to represent the mean, interquartile range (IQR), and 90% range. I explained that this format is typically seen as a boxplot, indicating the median and IQR, leading to possible misconceptions when presenting the intended data. I suggested clarifying the visual mapping in captions and distinguishing it from a traditional boxplot using various graphical elements. Additionally, I offered specific R/ggplot techniques for creating a custom summary graphic that conveys the desired information clearly. Finally, I recommended evaluating the audience's statistical literacy to gauge the appropriateness of the chosen representation and offered further assistance in coding if needed.
